# Compiled artifacts of the C assembler. Regenerate with: cd mac-c && make
# EVERYTHING generated now lands in mac-c/build/ - objects and both
# executables (mac, test_mac). `make clean` removes the whole directory.
mac-c/build/

# Build/ is OUTPUT ONLY - every file in it is regenerated by `make build`
# (mac-c/Makefile + scripts/build/*.sh). Only Build/README.md, which explains
# the layout, is tracked. The working bring-up disc set (Build/bringup/) is
# created by `make prepare` and is disposable like everything else here.
Build/*
!Build/README.md

# Per-machine Claude Code guidance - not part of the repository.
CLAUDE.md
